# conf/gone.list — what the fleet deleted on purpose, and must not come back (T537, EPIC T516 R3).
# The ONE list; bin/gone-selftest.sh reads it and reds on any of these back in the tree.
#
#   <kind> <thing> <ticket> [<scope>]
#
#   path  <p>     no file or directory at <p> (relative to the repo root)
#   func  <name>  no definition of <name> in code (sh · python · go · ts/js)
#   word  <tok>   <tok> on no code line (whole word; comments, prose, docs/ and
#                 selftests are not scanned; `gone-ok: <why>` keeps one line)
#   key   <NAME>  a word, and not a key of conf/fleet.conf.reference
#   <ticket>      #<issue> or T<n> — what deleted it
#   <scope>       optional path prefix narrowing a func / word / key (default: all)
#
# A PR that deletes a feature adds its lines here. Bringing one back on purpose
# deletes its line, and the PR says why. A note goes on a comment line above.

# --- the old two-pane client (#4423): the thin client is the only one ---------
